WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.750
Now sewage.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:09.925
If your boat has an installed toilet, she needs a Coast Guard certified marine sanitation device, and there are three types.

3
00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:13.875
Type one is a flow-through device that treats the sewage.

4
00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:18.700
The treated effluent can be discharged, outside no-discharge zones.

5
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:22.350
It’s limited to boats sixty-five feet and under.

6
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.325
Type two treats to a higher standard.

7
00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:29.800
Same rule: treated effluent, outside no-discharge zones.

8
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.425
Type three is a holding tank.

9
00:00:32.675 --> 00:00:38.925
You empty it at a pump-out station, or discharge it untreated only more than three miles offshore.

10
00:00:39.175 --> 00:00:44.425
And then there are no-discharge zones, which include the whole Florida Keys sanctuary.

11
00:00:44.675 --> 00:00:46.725
What can you discharge there?

12
00:00:47.725 --> 00:00:49.225
Nothing.

13
00:00:49.475 --> 00:00:51.225
Treated or not.

14
00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:54.500
And the Y-valve has to be secured closed.
